Sooner or later, somebody is going to bring up combat anyway.

00:31:36.720 --> 00:31:38.340
So let's just talk about this.

00:31:39.160 --> 00:31:45.200
It's different in the sense of it takes a whole new meaning to turn-based gameplay here.

00:31:45.200 --> 00:31:49.460
Because your combat is actually sort of like an SRPG.

00:31:49.620 --> 00:31:52.300
Where everybody moves one at a time.

00:31:52.300 --> 00:31:55.420
And you decide what they're going to do individually.

00:31:55.460 --> 00:31:57.380
And then the opponents go.

00:31:57.640 --> 00:32:01.880
And so there's this map with all of your characters, all of their characters.

00:32:02.080 --> 00:32:06.700
And terrain. And you have to kind of figure out what's the best way to approach the situation.

00:32:06.700 --> 00:32:08.260
Given the number of enemies.

00:32:08.580 --> 00:32:11.080
The location. The types of enemies.

00:32:11.500 --> 00:32:15.840
Your party. There's a lot of information on every single combat screen.

00:32:16.100 --> 00:32:18.580
This is not just choose your attack.

00:32:18.580 --> 00:32:23.060
And then an RNG generator to figure out if it lands or not.

00:32:23.220 --> 00:32:24.420
That still happens.

00:32:24.420 --> 00:32:27.960
But there's this whole where you are on the board.

00:32:28.200 --> 00:32:29.820
And where everybody else is.

00:32:30.500 --> 00:32:31.400
Real quick.

00:32:31.580 --> 00:32:34.180
Can you define SRPG?

