00:33:25.020 --> 00:33:26.480
And that really makes these drag.

00:33:28.240 --> 00:33:31.660
I don't know if you want to elaborate on your feelings there.

00:33:32.060 --> 00:33:34.100
I mean I felt the same way.

00:33:34.220 --> 00:33:38.780
I mean they definitely. I hadn't really thought of them adding move and attack into like one turn.

00:33:39.020 --> 00:33:41.200
I think that's definitely like a plus.

00:33:41.200 --> 00:33:43.360
I don't have any argument against that.

00:33:43.540 --> 00:33:45.440
But you know I was initially like the same way.

00:33:45.520 --> 00:33:46.440
I was like okay this sucks.

00:33:46.520 --> 00:33:49.400
Like having to. It's taking so long to get close to anyone and whatever.

00:33:50.700 --> 00:33:52.560
But as I kind of started to.

00:33:52.560 --> 00:33:53.780
To look at it that way.

00:33:53.900 --> 00:33:55.020
And like plan around that.

00:33:55.320 --> 00:33:56.300
It did get sort of fun.

00:33:56.420 --> 00:34:00.580
Kind of like planning. Okay like I want my character to end up this close to that enemy.

00:34:00.760 --> 00:34:03.600
And I want this other character that's healing everyone to stay back.

00:34:03.780 --> 00:34:04.940
And I want this person to be.

00:34:05.200 --> 00:34:07.100
Who's a ranged attacker to be.

00:34:07.360 --> 00:34:08.340
You know on.

00:34:09.220 --> 00:34:11.200
The same plane as like this enemy.

00:34:11.460 --> 00:34:13.440
So we can attack like at the same time.

00:34:13.920 --> 00:34:15.760
All the while staying out of like.

00:34:15.980 --> 00:34:18.100
There are spaces because of the way it works.

00:34:18.240 --> 00:34:22.160
There are spaces where. Where sometimes you might be able to get hit by two enemies.

00:34:22.360 --> 00:34:23.680
And not be able to hit either of them.

00:34:23.940 --> 00:34:25.220
So you're going to stay out of these like spaces.

00:34:25.380 --> 00:34:26.480
That are diagonal to an enemy.

00:34:26.660 --> 00:34:28.580
Because basically they can attack diagonally.

