Well, I'll say that everything at least that I've been saying and I do have a lot of I did really like this game in some aspects.

01:05:24.480 --> 01:05:25.960
I have a lot of good things to say about this game.

01:05:25.960 --> 01:05:31.240
But all the negative things I'm saying about this game, I'm saying with the exploit, I only played it with the exploit.

01:05:31.440 --> 01:05:36.460
So like even with the exploit, like there are a lot, there's a lot of flaws.

01:05:36.460 --> 01:05:37.500
There's still a challenge there. Yeah.

01:05:38.640 --> 01:05:41.380
Okay, but here's the thing about exploits in games.

01:05:41.520 --> 01:05:52.340
There is a way to make a good game that has not even like an actual exploit, but just something that's like, oh, well, this is just the game on easy mode.

01:05:52.480 --> 01:05:55.680
And it all goes back to a little game I like to call Super Mario World.

01:05:55.960 --> 01:06:02.260
All right. Where the main power up of the cape, some people will tell you that the cape is just too powerful.

01:06:02.380 --> 01:06:06.800
You can just fly over the levels and do all your things and stuff like that.

01:06:06.880 --> 01:06:14.440
And that's true. But I was also able to respect that game enough to be like, this game is fun without the cape.

01:06:14.580 --> 01:06:23.460
Like I want to play these levels and I want to beat them without the cape so that I can actually like play them as Mario because that part of the game is also fun.

01:06:23.460 --> 01:06:34.140
I would argue as somebody who played with and without the exploit, it is not as fun to play this game when you're actually doing the correct way.

01:06:34.380 --> 01:06:35.460
Yeah. I agree.

01:06:35.920 --> 01:06:40.800
All right. Let's move on for a second because it seems like we're getting into an agreement there.

01:06:40.800 --> 01:06:41.740
We're getting into the weeds here. So I want to –

01:06:41.740 --> 01:06:43.520
Yeah. We don't want to agree with this.

01:06:43.740 --> 01:06:45.320
And agree with this. I want to leave an agreement.

01:06:45.560 --> 01:06:48.680
You know, like I think that that's good because a lot of times on this show we just fight the whole time.

01:06:48.760 --> 01:06:50.760
I love fighting. So let's agree. Let's agree to agree.

01:06:51.200 --> 01:06:52.280
Can you agree with me? I agree.

01:06:52.780 --> 01:06:55.320
Okay. Thank you. Caves and dungeons.

01:06:55.680 --> 01:06:57.640
All right. Let's talk about it.

01:06:57.640 --> 01:06:59.820
There is a different system here.

01:07:00.800 --> 01:07:05.680
It's all of a sudden a first-person 3D.

01:07:05.680 --> 01:07:06.780
Dungeon crawler.

01:07:07.140 --> 01:07:08.760
Yeah. Dungeon crawler.

01:07:09.220 --> 01:07:18.980
But like, you know, more like with wireframe design because there's not enough information here to really discern where you are in first person.

01:07:18.980 --> 01:07:29.280
Not that we were expecting anything amazing, but I think even games like the Goonies had more detail on their set building.

01:07:29.400 --> 01:07:32.800
That's true. Than Ultima is offering here.

01:07:33.040 --> 01:07:38.520
But Ultima is also offering a much larger exploration than Goonies was offering.

01:07:38.600 --> 01:07:41.360
So I can understand that they're saying, well, here's the tradeback.

01:07:41.480 --> 01:07:43.920
You know, we'll give you a crazy big dungeon.

01:07:44.200 --> 01:07:46.160
We just can't make it look as pretty.

01:07:46.420 --> 01:07:47.480
I don't know, man.

01:07:48.800 --> 01:07:50.460
Okay. So the dungeons are big.

01:07:51.540 --> 01:07:53.000
Huge. They're huge.

01:07:53.160 --> 01:08:02.960
Yes. But is that like, okay, we made them look less pretty so we can make them these huge megaliths that are the same everywhere.

01:08:03.300 --> 01:08:08.820
And there's a couple – I mean there's a bunch of treasure chests everywhere with the same stuff in them.

01:08:08.840 --> 01:08:15.840
And there's a couple fountains everywhere just to, like, you know, maybe trick you or give you some water – some water.

01:08:15.980 --> 01:08:17.160
Give you some life back.

01:08:17.480 --> 01:08:20.500
And then there's going to be these random battles everywhere.

01:08:20.840 --> 01:08:22.560
Like, did it need to be that big?

01:08:22.820 --> 01:08:24.460
Well, Sean, you fell into my trap.

01:08:24.660 --> 01:08:30.720
You fell right into my trap of, again, another thing where the developers came up with this system, right?

01:08:30.720 --> 01:08:41.840
You know, let's just make it a huge adventure game where you've got this cave that's so big that you might get lost in it and lose your save file and have to start all over again.

01:08:41.840 --> 01:08:50.080
Like, let's really just, like, show people how hard it is to go, you know, trekking through the world of Ultima.

01:08:50.400 --> 01:08:52.980
And I'm kind of like, no, pass.

01:08:53.220 --> 01:09:00.980
Like, I don't want to explore your gigantic labyrinth that could cause me to, like, soft lock my game if I'm not careful.

01:09:01.080 --> 01:09:02.080
Now, that can't actually happen.

01:09:02.080 --> 01:09:06.600
But I think when you die in the dungeon, correct me if I'm wrong, you just go back to being British, right?

01:09:06.600 --> 01:09:09.100
You go back to being British, right? Yeah. Lord British to you.

01:09:09.520 --> 01:09:12.720
Let me say something positive about the dungeons.

01:09:13.760 --> 01:09:16.180
So, we've seen this done a couple other times.

01:09:16.340 --> 01:09:17.220
What was it? Golgo 13.

01:09:18.060 --> 01:09:22.100
I feel like there were one or two others that tried to do this, like, 3D maze sort of thing.

01:09:23.060 --> 01:09:23.880
This, I think...

01:09:23.880 --> 01:09:26.920
Yes. I think this was the best iteration.

01:09:27.260 --> 01:09:28.180
This was the best try.

01:09:28.380 --> 01:09:35.420
Because this was the first time that I remember seeing this, like, 3D environment and not really ever losing my bearings.

01:09:35.600 --> 01:09:36.480
There was a compass.

01:09:36.880 --> 01:09:38.480
Yeah. Was there not a compass in other games?

01:09:38.640 --> 01:09:39.740
I was trying to remember. Well, I don't know.

01:09:39.740 --> 01:09:45.140
I think this is the only one that I really, like, saw, like, oh, I'm facing north.

01:09:45.160 --> 01:09:46.180
I get it. Right.

01:09:46.440 --> 01:09:49.700
Yeah. And I didn't get disoriented or lost in that way.

01:09:49.780 --> 01:09:51.480
Like, okay, wait. Did I come from this way?

01:09:51.540 --> 01:09:53.040
Did I come from that way? Which way am I facing now?

01:09:53.200 --> 01:09:54.260
Obviously, just because there's a compass.

01:09:54.640 --> 01:10:01.140
And that made it more fun for me to kind of try and solve the maze and try and backtrack and figure out, like, where did I come from?

01:10:01.220 --> 01:10:06.020
Try and, like, map it out in my head or maybe, like, write it on a piece of paper and, like, map out where I've been and where I've come from.

01:10:08.500 --> 01:10:15.140
But I feel like with everything this game does right, it does something that kind of hurts that, like, positive point.

01:10:15.140 --> 01:10:30.140
And for reasons I can't fathom, we've seen other games do this also, most, if not all, of these dungeons require you to many, many times understand that a wall is not really a wall.

01:10:30.400 --> 01:10:34.600
You'll run into a dead end or you'll just look to your left on the wall that you've been walking along the whole time.

01:10:34.600 --> 01:10:39.980
And at one point, it's actually a secret doorway that if you walk through, there's no wall really there.

01:10:40.160 --> 01:10:41.140
And you have to go through it.

01:10:41.260 --> 01:10:45.320
You have no idea where these secret walls are, but they're everywhere.

01:10:46.420 --> 01:11:00.920
And that makes it – that completely negates the fact that they made these, like, functioning mazes that I can get my bearings in because it still found a way to make it impossible for me to really figure it out without just trying every possible tile.

01:11:01.820 --> 01:11:09.780
Yeah. And my – so my complaint wasn't so much that it was just as disorienting.

01:11:09.920 --> 01:11:11.060
I know what I'm saying.

01:11:11.720 --> 01:11:13.760
I'm not saying that you were implying that.

01:11:14.420 --> 01:11:16.740
I'm not saying that you were implying that I was implying that.

01:11:16.760 --> 01:11:18.120
It was just that it was featureless.

01:11:18.120 --> 01:11:21.300
And, like, yeah, these secret walls are features, I guess.

01:11:22.900 --> 01:11:35.180
But if you're going to make eight levels of a maze, maybe put some other interesting things in them than treasure chests with gold in them.

01:11:35.340 --> 01:11:37.180
Yeah. I mean, I totally agree with that point too.

01:11:37.820 --> 01:11:45.540
Yeah. But, you know, Joe, you mentioned there's this – you know, for everything that's good, there's one bad.

01:11:45.720 --> 01:11:46.520
It's like, no.

01:11:46.700 --> 01:11:49.800
It's like for everything that's good, there's a lot of bad.

01:11:50.700 --> 01:11:52.720
And there is some good stuff in this game.

01:11:52.720 --> 01:11:54.080
I'm not trying to knock it.

01:11:54.180 --> 01:11:57.680
I think there is something to enjoy and there were kind of moments where I was surprised.

01:11:58.320 --> 01:12:02.960
For instance, the first time I went into one of these dungeons, I was like, wow, it's first-person 3D.

01:12:03.080 --> 01:12:03.940
That's surprising.

01:12:04.320 --> 01:12:07.200
Shouldn't have been considering how hard everything was up until that point.

01:12:07.200 --> 01:12:15.460
But, you know, it's more like these things that they do right are, you know, glimmers of light.

01:12:15.600 --> 01:12:17.840
You're like, oh, maybe they've figured it out.

01:12:17.940 --> 01:12:23.840
And then you just remember, you know, what you're doing and how long you've been playing and what you could have been playing instead.

01:12:24.620 --> 01:12:28.460
And you have this issue that I've been having all along.

01:12:28.560 --> 01:12:30.860
But, again, with the caves, why?

01:12:31.040 --> 01:12:32.540
Why first-person 3D?

01:12:32.720 --> 01:12:34.580
Why couldn't this be in 2D?

01:12:34.580 --> 01:12:40.080
They already – it's not like it's never been done before to make 2D dungeons.

01:12:40.360 --> 01:12:43.220
Most of the NES games we play, the dungeons take place in 2D.

01:12:43.440 --> 01:12:46.740
Heck, make this one a platformer, right?

01:12:46.900 --> 01:12:48.960
Now, all of a sudden, you have to use –

01:12:48.960 --> 01:12:51.180
Stop trying to make this game a platformer, Mike.

01:12:51.280 --> 01:12:52.080
Get the zapper.

01:12:52.160 --> 01:12:53.080
Stop it. Get the zapper.

01:12:53.280 --> 01:12:58.120
Get Rob. But even the fact that, like, the dungeons are dark, right?

01:12:58.280 --> 01:13:01.300
Like, okay, makes sense again, world building and everything like that.

01:13:01.440 --> 01:13:02.680
Who's this game for?

01:13:03.860 --> 01:13:05.680
Dungeons are dark, world building.

01:13:05.720 --> 01:13:06.780
Dungeons are dark, right, right.

01:13:07.280 --> 01:13:08.760
You know? No, because think about it.

01:13:08.860 --> 01:13:13.980
Like, there are some caves you go into, again, in a game like Pokemon where it's like only certain ones require Flash.

01:13:13.980 --> 01:13:15.060
And it's like, why is that?

01:13:15.220 --> 01:13:17.260
Like, wouldn't all the caves be dark?

01:13:18.780 --> 01:13:21.620
So, you know, this is interesting that all the dungeons are dark in this game.

01:13:21.760 --> 01:13:23.000
They chose to commit to it.

01:13:23.120 --> 01:13:27.760
I love it. However, it's going to require you to constantly use spells.

01:13:27.940 --> 01:13:31.100
And if you don't have the MP for it, then you have to use torches.

01:13:31.120 --> 01:13:32.980
And if you don't have that, you're just going in the dark.

01:13:34.100 --> 01:13:37.640
You know, you need to constantly spam this stuff over and over and over again.

01:13:37.720 --> 01:13:38.560
Like, those things diminish.

01:13:38.800 --> 01:13:42.400
The spell is cast, and it's not like it's good until you leave the dungeon.

01:13:42.420 --> 01:13:43.880
It's done when it's done.

01:13:43.880 --> 01:13:50.800
It's done. So, it's just another thing where it's like, I shouldn't be able to think of this many examples of things while I'm playing a game.

01:13:50.800 --> 01:13:53.880
I should be able to just enjoy the game, not saying, like, why do I want this?

01:13:53.960 --> 01:13:54.760
Why do I want that?

01:13:54.960 --> 01:13:56.800
I don't consider that a negative, honestly.

01:13:57.740 --> 01:14:02.320
That gives me a little bit of, like, the satisfaction of, like, okay, having to prepare.

01:14:02.720 --> 01:14:03.820
Okay, I'm going to go in this dungeon.

01:14:03.820 --> 01:14:05.100
I'm not just going to go walk to the dungeon.

01:14:05.260 --> 01:14:07.880
Like, you know, I'm trying to immerse myself.

01:14:08.000 --> 01:14:10.020
So, like, well, I better go into town and pick up some torches.

01:14:10.240 --> 01:14:11.260
And I better have some tents.

01:14:11.380 --> 01:14:12.960
And I better stock up, you know, on food.

01:14:12.960 --> 01:14:14.760
Food, which I thought was really stupid at first.

01:14:14.920 --> 01:14:19.580
But then, like, as time went on, I was like, well, it's a nice little break from fighting the same enemy over and over again.

01:14:19.700 --> 01:14:23.700
And it, like, gives me something to, like, immerse myself.

01:14:24.160 --> 01:14:25.760
Yeah, it's like it's a little immersion.

01:14:25.900 --> 01:14:28.200
Like, it gives me a reason to care that I got to a town.

01:14:28.340 --> 01:14:29.940
I'm like, oh, great. I'm at a town.

01:14:30.000 --> 01:14:35.660
I can go pick up the supplies I need, which are different depending on what I'm going to do next.

01:14:35.660 --> 01:14:37.540
I mean, there's not a ton of those things.

01:14:37.700 --> 01:14:42.500
But you need torches. You might want sand if you're going to fight some high-level enemies and you want to slow them down.

01:14:42.640 --> 01:14:45.780
You just got to think about, like, your money management in that sense, too.

01:14:45.920 --> 01:14:48.260
And I actually thought that that helped the immersion a little bit.

01:14:48.740 --> 01:14:59.820
But if this is a game like Fallout New Vegas where there's, like, a survival mode, right, where, like, you know, you have to eat food, you have to manage everything about yourself, and, you know, you die and that's it, right?

01:15:00.100 --> 01:15:11.260
Like, if it is a survival mode game, I'm into that because the overall, like, game is working for me and is fun and the idea of surviving in that world is fun.

01:15:11.520 --> 01:15:13.900
I'm not, at this point, definitely.

01:15:14.120 --> 01:15:16.960
I mean, now I'm, like, who knows how many hours in before I've entered a dungeon.

01:15:16.960 --> 01:15:23.180
I am not sold that I want to prepare and slog through all these additional dungeons.

01:15:23.440 --> 01:15:26.620
I don't want to do that at this point in the game.

01:15:26.780 --> 01:15:31.060
If you would have introduced that earlier, I would have maybe taken it a little more seriously.

01:15:31.240 --> 01:15:33.060
But at this point, I'm exhausted.

01:15:33.460 --> 01:15:45.740
I don't want to have to constantly cast spells and bring all this stuff and figure out, like, okay, I think I already went down this corridor before seven times, you know?

01:15:45.740 --> 01:15:50.840
I know this is sounding like I'm whining and I am putting on a bit of, you know, a character here.

01:15:51.180 --> 01:16:02.900
But bear with me because I think the overall point is is that every new thing that happens in this game, I am left saying, well, why couldn't they just do thing I want instead?

01:16:02.900 --> 01:16:07.340
And that doesn't happen with every game we play.

01:16:07.340 --> 01:16:09.940
And it definitely doesn't happen with every bad game we play.

01:16:10.060 --> 01:16:14.840
Like, a lot of games, I'll just admit, I'm like, these aren't for me or these just aren't good games, you know?

01:16:14.940 --> 01:16:16.360
But I don't think of, like, alternatives.

01:16:16.640 --> 01:16:21.300
For this game, it seems like everything that I don't like, I do have an alternative answer for.

01:16:21.420 --> 01:16:25.120
And I am not saying that I am better than the people who made Ultimate Exit.

01:16:25.120 --> 01:16:27.780
Well, I agree. Go ahead, Joe.

01:16:27.980 --> 01:16:30.980
I would just say, so what is your alternative answer to the torch thing?

01:16:31.080 --> 01:16:34.020
Just not having torches and just having it be lit up the whole time?

01:16:34.660 --> 01:16:39.600
I think there could be a torch that, you know, when you have that torch, right?

01:16:39.600 --> 01:16:44.060
Like, it's at the front of the dungeon or whatever, and you bring, you know, you have that torch.

01:16:44.140 --> 01:16:46.400
And that's, like, that's your party's torch.

01:16:46.540 --> 01:16:47.360
There's four of you.

01:16:47.580 --> 01:16:49.060
One person can hold the torch.

01:16:49.620 --> 01:16:52.440
And you can grab more torches throughout the cave.

01:16:52.560 --> 01:16:55.640
Like, somebody had to explore those caves before you.

01:16:55.780 --> 01:16:59.260
So there must be, you know, like, it's not, they're not really, like, caves.

01:16:59.400 --> 01:17:04.340
They are layered dungeons that have, like, stuff inside them.

01:17:04.420 --> 01:17:05.520
So clearly people have been there.

01:17:05.520 --> 01:17:14.960
So I don't think if, you know, if that's the answer, I would actually say I'd go back to my 2D response of, like, I don't see why these dungeons even have to be in first person.

01:17:16.800 --> 01:17:20.940
But, you know, I think the realism is, again, great.

01:17:21.060 --> 01:17:24.980
Like, you know, I've been saying that this whole time of, like, who is this game really for?

01:17:24.980 --> 01:17:29.340
And the fact that they give you all these choices is undeniably a decision that they've made.

01:17:29.460 --> 01:17:33.400
They want you to feel like you're in control of everything that happens.

01:17:34.440 --> 01:17:36.820
I guess I've just had it.

01:17:37.220 --> 01:17:39.420
You know? Yeah, I mean, I don't, like, I'm submitting the control.

01:17:39.560 --> 01:17:42.200
I'm like, I'm done. So here's where I'm going to try and bridge the gap here.

01:17:42.480 --> 01:17:54.940
I agree that without these diminishing resources like food, like torches, not so much like MP because all you have to do is spin around in a circle and then you can cast light again.

01:17:55.900 --> 01:18:00.960
But without that, it sort of makes the dungeons feel a little less harrowing.

01:18:01.140 --> 01:18:12.660
What I would say, though, is that these specific things that you are preparing for, because preparation is a huge concept and it's a really big part of this game.

01:18:14.580 --> 01:18:16.680
It's just the way that it was executed.

01:18:16.960 --> 01:18:29.100
And, like, unlike Mike, I don't really know how you could go about it without just removing these features that would make this feel less like of a claustrophobic environment.

01:18:31.320 --> 01:18:48.620
But there just should have, if they did it in a different way, if, like, it was, if maybe if it was just a little more forgiving, like, if you did run out of torches, there could be some way to find some more while you're still, like, lost in the dark.

01:18:48.620 --> 01:18:49.440
I don't know.

01:18:51.720 --> 01:18:55.880
But it does, it is tedious in its current form.

01:18:56.060 --> 01:19:01.220
And I'm not, I guess I'm just not eloquent enough to put it in a way.

01:19:02.700 --> 01:19:04.380
Mike just says that he's kind of done.

01:19:04.620 --> 01:19:07.200
I don't have anything better to say than that, too.

01:19:08.320 --> 01:19:17.140
I mean, I will say that, you know, I definitely don't think that this is the best and most interesting, like, types of preparation they could put in their game.

01:19:17.140 --> 01:19:21.580
Of course, yeah. But I do think that having it is better than not having it.

01:19:21.680 --> 01:19:26.020
And I actually still do sort of think that, like, it shouldn't be more forgiving.

01:19:26.140 --> 01:19:35.620
Like, if you didn't bring enough torches or don't have a spell, then, like, yeah, you know, you should, you know, there should be a consequence where it's like, oh, shit, I'm going to die here.

01:19:35.620 --> 01:19:36.700
Oh, it should definitely be detrimental.

01:19:37.560 --> 01:19:40.600
Yeah. But, yeah, you're right.

01:19:40.780 --> 01:19:42.120
I actually agree with you there.

01:19:42.600 --> 01:19:45.360
Yeah. Yeah, I mean, like, yeah.

01:19:45.360 --> 01:19:48.580
I think for me, it's just like the overall, it's still pretty shallow.

01:19:48.740 --> 01:19:55.440
I want more in-depth versions of that or more stuff to do that with if that's going to be, like, the direction the game goes.

01:19:55.580 --> 01:19:57.300
But I do think, yeah, I don't know.

01:19:57.360 --> 01:20:00.640
Just taking it away, I feel like, makes it less interesting for me.

01:20:00.740 --> 01:20:02.200
But I guess it's just a preference as well.

01:20:02.200 --> 01:20:09.840
There should be rats that, you know, just like they run across your feet and they give you a disease.

01:20:10.100 --> 01:20:15.080
And then it's just like you have to get back to the hospital before, you know, before the disease kills you.

01:20:15.080 --> 01:20:18.260
Well, that sort of does happen. I mean, you open a chest and you get a disease and you have to get back to the hospital.

01:20:18.260 --> 01:20:21.840
I think that's funny because that happened on my very first playthrough of the game.

01:20:22.080 --> 01:20:23.940
One of my characters caught a cold.

01:20:24.040 --> 01:20:25.540
Yeah, caught a cold for the first chest.

01:20:25.540 --> 01:20:27.180
I couldn't find a fountain.

01:20:27.460 --> 01:20:29.240
So I was like, I'm dead.

01:20:29.460 --> 01:20:31.320
Like, this is, I have to reset the game.

01:20:31.320 --> 01:20:35.320
I don't know where a fountain is and that's the only way to cure a cold, apparently.

01:20:35.800 --> 01:20:36.960
I think you can go to the hospital.

01:20:36.960 --> 01:20:37.760
You can go to the doctor.

01:20:38.120 --> 01:20:39.620
Yeah. You silly goose.

01:20:40.080 --> 01:20:41.220
I didn't go to the doctor.

01:20:41.340 --> 01:20:45.860
So I just reset that game and didn't get a cold until later on after that.

01:20:46.000 --> 01:20:49.480
But I think that's so funny that, like, my first experience in this game was getting a cold.

01:20:49.680 --> 01:20:51.740
And I'm like, oh, you want to be more real?

01:20:51.740 --> 01:20:55.740
The rats give you the plague and you have to escape the cave before you die.

01:20:56.300 --> 01:20:58.100
Hey, I mean, that's somebody's game.

01:20:58.820 --> 01:21:13.420
Well, something that, something that is sort of on the same, same page as what we're talking about is the way that your character is like, your character dying is detrimental also.

01:21:13.640 --> 01:21:19.440
It's not like, oh, I'll use a quick revive or I'll run to the Pokemon Center, you know, and heal my party.

01:21:19.440 --> 01:21:28.120
Yeah. And I, because of how much of a pain it was, I really, really fought very hard to not let any of my characters ever die.

01:21:28.300 --> 01:21:30.600
Like, after like one or two and I switched to new characters.

01:21:30.700 --> 01:21:32.620
Once I had the characters I was going to use for the rest of the game.

01:21:32.660 --> 01:21:35.380
It's very expensive. I was like, yeah, do not let the characters ever die.

01:21:35.520 --> 01:21:37.120
Always make sure they have enough food.

01:21:37.400 --> 01:21:41.160
Always heal, you know, and make sure that they're all like high levels.

01:21:41.320 --> 01:21:44.060
And I succeeded for most of the game.

01:21:44.660 --> 01:21:46.900
I got to the point where I had everything you needed.

01:21:47.040 --> 01:21:53.300
There's a lot of like errands to run before you can go into the final, the final dungeon or the castle.

01:21:54.400 --> 01:21:55.860
And I got everything I needed.

01:21:56.080 --> 01:22:00.520
And I was, and I was, the last thing I was getting, there's some cards you have to get in Ambrosia.

01:22:00.600 --> 01:22:02.260
I was getting those. I got those final ones.

01:22:03.280 --> 01:22:06.860
And two of my characters, or three of my characters died because I realized I'd run out of food.

01:22:06.860 --> 01:22:12.180
And I was like, oh shit, like, I got to get back to town fast before my fourth character dies.

01:22:12.600 --> 01:22:17.000
You know, so I use the, you know, you get like these heart compasses that transport you back to the main town.

01:22:17.240 --> 01:22:18.880
I use that. I get in there.

01:22:19.360 --> 01:22:22.320
I get some food real quick to give to my remaining character.

01:22:22.420 --> 01:22:26.320
But I have no money left because I just spent it all on upgrades in Ambrosia.

01:22:26.720 --> 01:22:28.780
So I have to go, this is a really long story, sorry.

01:22:28.980 --> 01:22:33.300
But I have to go and fight with my one remaining.

01:22:33.300 --> 01:22:39.340
I have to fight with my one remaining character as much as I can to get enough money to revive people because it costs, I think, 500 gold.

01:22:39.560 --> 01:22:41.100
Then I go to the doctor to revive.

01:22:41.240 --> 01:22:42.280
First time I've ever tried it.

01:22:42.520 --> 01:22:44.900
Failed. And he says, he says, no, it doesn't fail.

01:22:44.900 --> 01:22:47.580
He says, I'll see what I can do.

01:22:47.720 --> 01:22:49.800
And then he comes back and says, you took too long.

01:22:50.500 --> 01:22:51.520
You took too long.

01:22:51.680 --> 01:22:52.900
John, or no, Matt.

01:22:53.040 --> 01:22:54.280
They're all named after people I know too.

01:22:54.520 --> 01:22:56.020
Matt, my archer. He's like, you took too long.

01:22:56.160 --> 01:22:57.240
Matt has turned to dust.

01:22:58.240 --> 01:22:59.580
And there's no reviving him.

01:22:59.640 --> 01:23:02.720
This character I just spent like 40 hours building.

01:23:02.720 --> 01:23:04.860
And you just can't get him back.

01:23:05.120 --> 01:23:06.840
Oh, you can't. I had to go to an older save.

01:23:07.180 --> 01:23:09.100
Thank God I didn't save it after he had died.

01:23:09.280 --> 01:23:11.680
But then I was like, now I've got to do all this shit again?

01:23:12.840 --> 01:23:23.020
I'm not speaking from experience, but I'm speaking from somebody else's experience that you have to go to some place and go to a temple and they can turn them from ash back into person.

01:23:23.240 --> 01:23:24.400
Oh, I didn't know that.

01:23:24.480 --> 01:23:27.000
I really thought that it was like, oh, what's the, how long?

01:23:27.000 --> 01:23:29.160
But that's like 900 gold.

01:23:29.820 --> 01:23:30.620
So. Jeez.

01:23:31.040 --> 01:23:34.960
And like, how long does it take for them to turn to, like, how long do you have to get to the hospital?

01:23:35.040 --> 01:23:42.980
I have no idea. That's why I see it as like the doctor failed because I think it's, I think it's RNG whether it works or not.

01:23:43.700 --> 01:23:44.800
But maybe it's a time limit thing.

01:23:44.800 --> 01:23:45.840
Well, he still took my money.

01:23:45.960 --> 01:23:47.440
So I couldn't even try it again.

01:23:47.900 --> 01:23:49.160
Yeah. He still took your money.

01:23:49.280 --> 01:23:52.360
That's like, you know, it's medical malpractice.

01:23:52.480 --> 01:23:54.260
It's like, whatever. You still got a bill to pay.

01:23:54.600 --> 01:23:57.280
That was the most frustrating experience I had playing this game.

01:23:57.340 --> 01:24:01.660
And there were a lot of others, but that was definitely, because I was ready to go face the final challenge.

01:24:01.660 --> 01:24:03.260
I was ready to go beat the game, I thought.

01:24:03.420 --> 01:24:04.220
I mean, it probably wasn't.

01:24:04.220 --> 01:24:05.760
That is still a cool story, though.

01:24:06.340 --> 01:24:07.760
Yeah. I got that out of it.

01:24:08.240 --> 01:24:09.180
There is story to this game.

01:24:10.080 --> 01:24:10.920
Moment of clarity.

01:24:11.220 --> 01:24:19.680
Okay. I just want to let everyone know that everything Joe has been talking about for a while now are all awesome features.

01:24:19.680 --> 01:24:21.460
And he's right to be excited about them.

01:24:21.460 --> 01:24:28.080
And I'm not arguing that these are unique features in this game and that they're all good and stuff like that.

01:24:28.700 --> 01:24:38.780
The argument I've been making for a while now, and I just want to make it as clear as possible, is that this game has lost its good faith from me.

01:24:38.980 --> 01:24:40.760
Like, I'm done with it.

01:24:40.900 --> 01:24:45.820
At this point, I can't hide it anymore that I'm not going to have a good time.

01:24:45.820 --> 01:24:48.480
And now it's like, again, the preparation thing.

01:24:48.680 --> 01:24:55.200
If this was Legend of Zelda Breath of the Wild and you had to prepare for a cave or that island, right, where, like, they stripped you of everything.

01:24:55.340 --> 01:24:58.480
And now you're in this island and you have to just, like, regain everything.

01:24:58.660 --> 01:25:00.140
Like, that's such a cool moment in that game.

01:25:00.140 --> 01:25:02.580
But I'm there for it because I'm there for that game.

01:25:02.820 --> 01:25:04.240
I'm not here for this game.

01:25:04.240 --> 01:25:08.560
So when it tries to do something cute and new, all of a sudden I'm just angry.

01:25:08.740 --> 01:25:12.660
I'm just angry that it's, like, another new thing that I have to deal with.

01:25:12.740 --> 01:25:16.760
Like you were talking about, Joe, with party members dying.

01:25:17.000 --> 01:25:23.440
It's like that's a really deep system that they've created here of, like, death is somewhat permanent.

01:25:23.440 --> 01:25:25.820
And who knows if you're even going to be able to get them back.

01:25:25.820 --> 01:25:30.520
And then even if you can't get them back, then you have to do Sean's method of going to a temple and reviving them.

01:25:30.640 --> 01:25:34.100
Like, that could take who knows how many hours and who knows how much time.

01:25:34.780 --> 01:25:38.520
And we could debate whether it should take that many hours and that much time.

01:25:38.520 --> 01:25:42.040
Or if there's just, like, a faster way to do it that would still make the effect really cool.

01:25:42.460 --> 01:25:52.800
What I'm saying is, is, like, that mechanic in the scheme of this game, like, this game's scope is just so large.

01:25:52.800 --> 01:25:56.140
And it's offering you so much.

01:25:56.580 --> 01:26:01.700
But the problem is, is that nothing really syncs with each other in this game.

01:26:01.840 --> 01:26:07.560
There's so many things that are fighting me at all times to make me not want to continue to play the game.

01:26:07.700 --> 01:26:15.420
That ultimately I can't enjoy the systems because they're all kind of working against you to make sure that the game itself is harder.

01:26:15.640 --> 01:26:19.900
I think, like, I kind of see what you mentioned it before, too.

01:26:19.900 --> 01:26:31.500
It seems like the negative consequences of a lot of things sort of outweigh the positives that come out of playing the game correctly or well.

01:26:32.680 --> 01:26:36.980
So that, like, for every step forward you feel like there's two steps back.

01:26:37.380 --> 01:26:42.660
It just, that sort of, that reward and punishment is just out of balance.

01:26:43.200 --> 01:26:44.160
Right? Yeah.

01:26:44.420 --> 01:26:45.620
I'm with you on that, too.

01:26:45.620 --> 01:26:58.120
I mean, even with what I was just complaining about with the death thing, now knowing, I mean, I think if my character was gone forever, I probably would not ever really be able to, like, think that that was a good system.

01:26:58.120 --> 01:27:09.540
But now knowing that there is a way, and it seems like even more of a pain in the ass, to get him back from Ashes and go there, I don't think that that's terrible if I, yeah, if I were enjoying the rest of the game enough to want to do that.

01:27:09.900 --> 01:27:14.080
You know? Yeah. I think that would be okay if the positives were up there with that negative.

01:27:14.220 --> 01:27:16.940
Then it feels like, okay, I got to go on this journey to get my characters back.

01:27:16.960 --> 01:27:20.900
It's like a whole other game now to get my characters back because, like, you know, is it worth it?

01:27:20.900 --> 01:27:21.740
And, you know, that whole thing.

01:27:21.900 --> 01:27:22.720
But, yeah, you're right.

01:27:22.820 --> 01:27:33.180
It doesn't – all it does for me is make me cringe at the idea of spending, like, that many more hours grinding just to get the money I need to get my characters back.

01:27:33.380 --> 01:27:38.080
Yeah. Like, if the loop was more fun, then I would enjoy it more.

01:28:06.560 --> 01:28:08.980
And let's talk about management.

01:28:10.380 --> 01:28:18.720
The, you know, the gold, the food, just, you know, weapons and armor, like, how you manage your team throughout the game.

01:28:19.460 --> 01:28:30.960
The first thing that I had to do right away was transfer all my gold to one character because I couldn't stand having, you know, when you're shopping and they're like, who's making the purchase?

01:28:31.160 --> 01:28:32.300
And then who is it for?

01:28:32.500 --> 01:28:39.160
Like, it's like just put the first character, everybody give him all the money and then we'll just – no, seriously.

01:28:39.300 --> 01:28:40.920
And then this way he's, like, in the front of the party.

01:28:41.080 --> 01:28:45.920
He collects the money and then he's just, like, our banker for the system.

01:28:46.180 --> 01:28:49.200
Yeah, that's kind of it too. It's a little strange though, right?

01:28:49.360 --> 01:28:52.680
It's a little strange that gold even has to be – like, you're a party of four.

01:28:53.840 --> 01:29:00.740
It's another, you know, D&D thing that they're sticking to where, like, everybody has their own gold and they can spend it how they want.

01:29:00.740 --> 01:29:03.640
But you're all four characters in this scenario.

01:29:03.980 --> 01:29:07.580
Like, you're not playing with three other people.

01:29:07.720 --> 01:29:17.440
I think the proper way to play this game might be with the four people and hand the controller back and forth between each of you and you each control one character and make all those decisions.

01:29:17.440 --> 01:29:19.260
That's really funny. No.

01:29:19.800 --> 01:29:23.940
No, that's funny though because – no, because that would make the combat sections even longer.

01:29:24.200 --> 01:29:34.100
It would make the whole game – like, it would make everything so much longer because you have to – you know, it's like – it's crazy that we talked about combat maybe, like, an hour ago now.

01:29:34.100 --> 01:29:40.560
But we, like, just said that, yeah, they don't let you move and they don't let you attack in the same turn.

01:29:40.640 --> 01:29:41.820
And that was, like, it.

01:29:41.880 --> 01:29:44.500
But I need to let the viewers know, like, that is frustrating.

01:29:44.760 --> 01:29:46.700
That is so crazy. It's such a huge thing.

01:29:47.160 --> 01:29:50.000
You, like, you move and then you – done.

01:29:50.140 --> 01:30:02.280
Like, that's your turn. And then God forbid, like, what if you – there's, like, something where you can accidentally choose – you press a button and then you no longer get the option to it.

01:30:02.280 --> 01:30:06.480
Oh, yeah. If you make the wrong input, it's just like, oh, that's your turn then.

01:30:06.620 --> 01:30:08.520
Like, you just risk the skip turn button.

01:30:08.540 --> 01:30:09.520
You made a mistake.

01:30:09.520 --> 01:30:15.700
And if you open a menu or one of the menus, you open the menu and you're like, oh, no, I want to back out of that menu.

01:30:16.160 --> 01:30:19.240
It's like, okay, you can back out of that menu, but you're not doing anything else.

01:30:19.400 --> 01:30:20.460
We'll move on to the next character.

01:30:20.620 --> 01:30:23.900
It's like, why – you're allowing me to back out of the menu.

01:30:24.020 --> 01:30:25.560
Let me have my turn still.

01:30:26.240 --> 01:30:35.980
But, yes, Mike, look, on the topic of managing resources, this game should have just had a party coin purse and a party inventory.

01:30:35.980 --> 01:30:48.240
So you don't have to deal with hot swapping money and, like, all this, like, very minute, tedious stuff that really – it's not necessary at all.

01:30:48.720 --> 01:30:51.080
I'm just surprised that they put it in the game at all.

01:30:51.700 --> 01:30:53.020
Well, because think about it.

01:30:53.080 --> 01:30:55.700
If that character dies, then their money is gone too.

01:30:55.980 --> 01:30:57.440
But that's not how that would work.

01:30:57.660 --> 01:30:59.480
I think you've got their ashes.

01:30:59.540 --> 01:31:01.000
You've got their ashes still.

01:31:01.140 --> 01:31:02.460
I think you can take the money off of them.

01:31:03.640 --> 01:31:12.280
Exactly. Well, I can confirm because I had two and eventually three dead characters that you can take things from dead characters.

01:31:12.540 --> 01:31:18.920
So it's there. Like, even that, like, risk of punishment isn't even – it should have just been a party inventory system.

01:31:19.040 --> 01:31:25.000
Yeah. There's nothing that anyone can say to say that it makes sense this way as a one-player game.

01:31:25.000 --> 01:31:38.720
What I think it boils down to is that they had – they were creative enough to find ways to put all of these elements from, like, Dungeons & Dragons into a video game.

01:31:38.720 --> 01:31:46.380
But they weren't creative enough to, like, recognize the things that should change from, like, a tabletop RPG into a one-player video game.

01:31:46.380 --> 01:31:53.260
And they, like, left too many of those things exactly the same, like, as close to the way that they would be done in, like, Dungeons & Dragons.

01:31:53.260 --> 01:31:54.440
Yeah, taking them as givens, yeah.

01:31:54.620 --> 01:31:56.280
Yeah. I get it.

01:31:56.820 --> 01:31:58.840
But no. Well, if you think about it – right.

01:31:59.140 --> 01:32:02.880
No, it's true. If you think about it, like, that's what Final Fantasy excels at, right?

01:32:03.020 --> 01:32:05.460
It was also based off of Dungeons & Dragons.

01:32:05.460 --> 01:32:09.460
I mean, some of the enemies are, like, right from the books.

01:32:09.660 --> 01:32:14.720
So it's interesting that they were able to be like, okay, well, we have to adapt this thing.

01:32:14.880 --> 01:32:16.800
Like, maybe they were just afraid of being sued.

01:32:17.120 --> 01:32:20.480
But they were like, we have to, you know, figure out a way to make this a video game.

01:32:20.520 --> 01:32:31.300
I think that's a great point, Joe, is, like, they decided to just do their best translation of Dungeons & Dragons without thinking about why it might not work.

01:32:31.300 --> 01:32:40.280
And given that this is the third entry, I'm really interested to know, like, what were the – what was the bare bones-ness of the first and second one?

01:32:40.360 --> 01:32:42.740
Like, what does this one feature and prove?

01:32:42.740 --> 01:33:03.120
So the first – I think the first two, like, on the PCs or the computer versions of the first two are more of, like, that first-person, like, turn-based, like, typical of what we think of as Final Fantasy that, like, just take turns attacking each other.

01:33:03.200 --> 01:33:07.000
There's no, like, spatial component to battles.

01:33:08.440 --> 01:33:11.020
I think all the – maybe the resource stuff is all the same.

01:33:11.140 --> 01:33:13.580
I didn't play them, but I was looking at some of them.

01:33:13.800 --> 01:33:18.140
And the battle system, at least, is much more akin to what I was expecting out of this game.

01:33:18.340 --> 01:33:30.780
It's even weirder, actually, because then that makes – then that's, like – they decide – it was, like, a new idea for them to try and make it more, like, Dungeons & Dragons.

01:33:30.880 --> 01:33:32.020
I don't know. I mean, I guess that makes sense.

01:33:32.140 --> 01:33:35.540
They're trying to, you know, they're trying a new thing, but it's weird that they didn't, like – I don't know.

01:33:35.540 --> 01:33:45.200
It's weird that they came up with the idea of making everything so much more one-to-one with Dungeons & Dragons rather than, like, having gotten more experience in making video games and realizing what works for video games.

01:33:46.120 --> 01:33:49.900
I mean, I still think that, like, you know, moving around in combat works.

01:33:50.080 --> 01:33:53.960
I mean, I love playing XCOM and Fire Emblem and stuff like that.

01:33:54.060 --> 01:33:56.140
It's just that they did it wrong.

01:33:57.460 --> 01:33:59.260
So it's just an experimentation.

01:33:59.260 --> 01:34:02.900
I don't blame them for doing it, but it did hurt the product.

01:34:02.900 --> 01:34:07.620
All right, so let's get back to that thing that I keep saying, like, all right, man, you know, maybe we'll have this conversation.

01:34:07.740 --> 01:34:09.060
Let's have this conversation, okay?

01:34:10.180 --> 01:34:12.140
Who is this game for?

01:34:12.580 --> 01:34:21.900
It's definitely not for Bobby, you know, your seven-year-old cousin who's going to Toys R Us and he sees this game and he's, like, this one, right?

01:34:22.020 --> 01:34:23.620
It's, like, that's a mistake.

01:34:23.860 --> 01:34:26.660
Like, you know, should have bought Super Mario Bros., kid.

01:34:26.660 --> 01:34:27.960
You're in for a world of hurt now.

01:34:27.960 --> 01:34:31.580
Now, who is this game for when it comes to the NES?

01:34:31.820 --> 01:34:35.900
Obviously, like, you know, computer gamers were a breed of their own back then.

01:34:36.100 --> 01:34:41.960
So was this game obtuse on purpose?

01:34:42.500 --> 01:34:45.000
I don't think it was obtuse on purpose.

01:34:45.000 --> 01:34:53.180
I think that Bobby could be a prospective RPG player.

01:34:53.560 --> 01:35:07.500
Like, this is, like, what would have introduced him to this wild world of choice and consequence that RPGs are, or at least, like, Western RPGs are all about.

01:35:09.300 --> 01:35:16.500
I think that we see all of these faults and, like, all of these terrible systems.

01:35:17.940 --> 01:35:36.600
But what Bobby, and I love that we've just created this straw man here, Bobby just sees this land of adventure where he can steal a pirate ship and choose who gets to hold the money and talk to the people and go to the bar and talk to the bartender.

01:35:37.140 --> 01:35:44.360
Like, that's the experience that this kid is seeing or somebody that really enjoyed this game back then is experiencing.

01:35:44.360 --> 01:36:11.720
We have played so many RPGs that have expanded on combat and expanded on choice and consequence and immersion that we are really only seeing all of these terrible dungeon designs and this clunky inventory system and this sort of knee-capped battle system.

01:36:12.360 --> 01:36:18.840
Where I think that's just what we get for being exposed to the modern RPG.

01:36:20.200 --> 01:36:23.580
I think Bobby was their target audience.

01:36:23.960 --> 01:36:25.800
Yeah, I couldn't agree more.

01:36:25.920 --> 01:36:38.620
I mean, that's almost exactly what I was going to say about, like, it being a game for, maybe they were trying to make it a game for Dungeons & Dragons fans, but I think they ended up making a game that was the gateway for people to, like, get into that kind of world.

01:36:38.620 --> 01:36:40.900
That were trying to get into, like, Dungeons & Dragons and stuff.

01:36:41.180 --> 01:36:49.160
And, yeah, I do think in 19, what, 1989, there's a different approach to, like, looking at this game.

01:36:49.260 --> 01:36:52.840
And I think that, like, the right person really enjoys this game in 1989.

01:36:53.280 --> 01:36:54.580
Yeah, I totally agree.

01:36:54.800 --> 01:36:55.900
I agree with that.

01:36:55.980 --> 01:36:57.500
The right person enjoys this game.

01:36:57.620 --> 01:37:02.120
I just am worried that the right person wasn't really on the NES.

01:37:02.120 --> 01:37:07.120
And I imagine that most people who favored this game played it on, like, an Apple II.

01:37:07.900 --> 01:37:11.980
I do like, I like everybody's responses here because they all check out.

01:37:12.100 --> 01:37:15.300
I think there's no wrong answer here other than saying me.

01:37:15.720 --> 01:37:17.680
The game is definitely not right.

01:37:19.280 --> 01:37:21.860
But that's also, like, you know, that's a thing, too.

01:37:23.200 --> 01:37:26.300
You can enjoy systems within a game.

01:37:26.340 --> 01:37:27.460
I certainly did.

01:37:28.880 --> 01:37:30.780
Even the little details in this game, right?

01:37:30.960 --> 01:37:34.820
Like, there's the phases of the moon included in the HUD.

01:37:34.960 --> 01:37:38.340
And it's, like, I just appreciate that being there.

01:37:38.480 --> 01:37:41.400
It's, like, it adds – I know that it's, like, not that complicated.

01:37:41.480 --> 01:37:47.260
And it just, like, tells, you know, like, depending on the cycles of the moon, like, magical portals open up and stuff.

01:37:47.260 --> 01:37:50.340
But to me, that just adds a lot of mystery and intrigue.

01:37:51.180 --> 01:37:54.080
And the game has a lot of that going for it.

01:37:54.160 --> 01:37:57.000
And that was the stuff I really liked about it.

01:37:58.860 --> 01:38:00.000
You know, it's funny.

01:38:00.140 --> 01:38:04.900
It's, like, when you reveal, like, what the game is after the fact, right?

01:38:05.020 --> 01:38:08.720
So let's pull the curtain here for a minute.

01:38:08.720 --> 01:38:20.140
And after I play these games, I do an extensive amount of research on these games, too, to make sure that we can give the listeners, you know, the correct info but also, like, a substantial amount of info.

01:38:20.140 --> 01:38:42.920
And there is a difference between playing this game for five hours, playing this game for 20-plus hours, and then, like, also seeing this game via research by looking at maps and looking at strategy guides and reading old reviews and stuff like that.

01:38:43.900 --> 01:38:55.200
It's, like, the idea of a game that has such a tremendous scope while at the same time disappointing on delivery.

01:38:55.520 --> 01:39:00.980
There's something about that that I couldn't get over as I continued to play and research the game.

01:39:02.400 --> 01:39:05.600
It just felt like such a missed opportunity here.

01:39:06.400 --> 01:39:17.560
I think we're the kings of being in love with ideas that a lot of the games that we've been reviewing have been presenting to us and just being disappointed by the execution of them.

01:39:17.780 --> 01:39:23.480
I think that that's just sort of – that's just games in general.

01:39:24.540 --> 01:39:26.120
Right. Yeah, I agree.

01:39:26.300 --> 01:39:33.260
That feeling of going in the whirlpool and discovering Ambrosia after that weird, vague line, right?

01:39:33.320 --> 01:39:34.380
That's not helpful at all.

01:39:34.380 --> 01:39:35.500
You know, it's not helpful.

01:39:35.640 --> 01:39:36.980
You have no idea what it means.

01:39:37.100 --> 01:39:40.620
But then when you get there, you're like, oh, wow, this is really cool.

01:39:40.720 --> 01:39:43.860
And you don't know what could happen in that other world.

01:39:43.960 --> 01:39:46.300
Like, maybe the rest of the game takes place there.

01:39:46.520 --> 01:39:47.720
You know? Who knows?

01:39:49.640 --> 01:39:52.660
I like that sky's the limit thing.

01:39:53.200 --> 01:39:58.660
I hate when I actually feel limited by the game because the game is very imaginative.

01:39:58.660 --> 01:40:03.160
It does offer a lot of unique systems and opportunities.

01:40:04.380 --> 01:40:05.300
To experience.

01:40:05.680 --> 01:40:09.580
But then there's all these other things in this game that I don't want to do.

01:40:11.220 --> 01:40:12.500
I agree.

01:40:12.800 --> 01:40:16.860
I agree with both of these viewpoints.

01:40:19.300 --> 01:40:20.760
Let's talk magic.

01:40:21.300 --> 01:40:26.960
We really only talked about the undead spell, which is kind of funny because there is a whole magic system.

01:40:27.140 --> 01:40:31.440
And there's also like what kind of character you are is what kind of magic you get too.

01:40:31.600 --> 01:40:37.160
Like, you know, the wizard, the cleric, the – who am I forgetting?

01:40:37.400 --> 01:40:39.700
The alchemist, the ranger have some.

01:40:41.080 --> 01:40:42.700
Paladin? No.

01:40:42.960 --> 01:40:43.860
Okay. Paladin?

01:40:43.980 --> 01:40:45.280
No, I don't think so. I don't think so.

01:40:45.560 --> 01:40:47.580
But anyway, yeah. A lot of different characters get magic.

01:40:47.820 --> 01:40:51.440
And they have different kinds of magic spells that they could have at their disposal.

01:40:51.600 --> 01:40:58.660
I think the wizard is the only one who has the opportunity to potentially learn everyone else's spells as well as their own.

01:40:59.040 --> 01:40:59.860
I'm not sure exactly.

01:40:59.860 --> 01:41:01.780
Wait. I thought the wizard only learned –

01:41:01.780 --> 01:41:04.020
Only black magic.

01:41:04.380 --> 01:41:06.580
Intelligence magic. Oh, really?

01:41:06.660 --> 01:41:08.220
The wizard can't learn like cleric spells?

01:41:08.420 --> 01:41:12.000
And then the cleric is like the white magic version of the wizard.

01:41:12.620 --> 01:41:13.740
Got it. Okay. I don't know.

01:41:13.920 --> 01:41:15.620
Yeah, because I didn't experience this in my game.

01:41:15.720 --> 01:41:17.100
I just read it. But okay.

01:41:17.120 --> 01:41:20.360
That's good to know. So that would be the difference between those two though.

01:41:20.500 --> 01:41:21.380
White magic, black magic.

01:41:21.460 --> 01:41:32.640
Got it. And then all of these other magic users are just some variation of – some of them can do both.

01:41:32.840 --> 01:41:38.840
Some of them can do only one, but not the level of like those pure classes.

01:41:38.840 --> 01:41:42.920
But they have a bit more like standard attack power.

01:41:45.540 --> 01:41:52.520
And yeah, it's – but yeah, the cleric and the wizard are like the pure magic users on either end of those.

01:41:52.520 --> 01:41:53.860
Oh, right. Sorry. I remember now.

01:41:53.860 --> 01:41:56.560
Yes, it's magic power and willpower.

01:41:56.560 --> 01:41:59.120
That's the difference between these guys.

01:41:59.540 --> 01:42:00.580
For the most part.

01:42:00.720 --> 01:42:06.160
Yeah. The cleric has the – but I'm saying like the willpower is their version of white magic in this game.

01:42:07.000 --> 01:42:09.700
I mean, they still draw from MP, right?

01:42:10.240 --> 01:42:14.720
Yeah, yeah. So there's – yeah, there's intelligence and then wisdom.

01:42:15.980 --> 01:42:20.920
I guess like yeah, will would be wisdom and magic would be intelligence.

01:42:21.580 --> 01:42:31.060
Yeah, and I think like a wisdom-based – like a cleric whose magic is based on wisdom, the higher your wisdom level is, the higher MP you have.

01:42:31.880 --> 01:42:33.020
But I think if you were to –

01:42:33.020 --> 01:42:34.040
And higher level spells are available to you.

01:42:34.240 --> 01:42:43.580
Yeah, yeah. But then if you were to do a wizard and give him higher intelligence, it doesn't raise your MP because he works on intelligence rather than wisdom.

01:42:43.860 --> 01:42:45.860
Yeah, wisdom on a wizard does nothing.

01:42:46.960 --> 01:42:50.200
Yeah. And what do you think of that?

01:42:50.340 --> 01:42:55.740
Is that like a waste? Is that like designed as a funny throwaway that you should know that?

01:42:55.740 --> 01:43:02.380
And if you attribute character points to the wizard and wisdom, then like that's just your fault?

01:43:02.640 --> 01:43:03.480
I mean, yeah, it is.

01:43:03.720 --> 01:43:05.100
I actually hadn't really thought about the fact that it's a waste.

01:43:05.360 --> 01:43:09.680
That like he has the ability to get these attributes that don't do anything for him.

01:43:09.680 --> 01:43:11.080
It's entirely –

01:43:11.080 --> 01:43:16.660
I didn't notice that. Yeah, it's fully brought over from like tabletop RPGs.

01:43:16.840 --> 01:43:17.920
Like if –

01:43:19.480 --> 01:43:26.200
Not so much because like if you have a fighter that has like a wisdom skill, like they still have things that they can do with wisdom.

01:43:29.160 --> 01:43:36.340
But yeah, like if you were to give a fighter or barbarian any intelligence or wisdom, that is a throwaway.

01:43:36.340 --> 01:43:39.820
You're just dumping points because they can't use magic.

01:43:40.620 --> 01:44:19.760
Yeah. We've done extensive stuff on combat, management, dungeons, exploration.

01:44:20.260 --> 01:44:31.740
Now it's time for the NPCs and the towns, you know, kind of like where you find out about your questing and what you'll do next if you're lucky enough to decipher what they mean.

01:44:31.740 --> 01:44:39.740
And, you know, right off the bat, the only thing that – and I should just be able to get over this because it's the limitations of the console itself.

01:44:40.100 --> 01:44:45.060
But it is kind of interesting how they display the town, right?

01:44:45.240 --> 01:44:48.720
Like they can't show you the entire screen all at once.

01:44:49.680 --> 01:44:54.160
Some of the – some of like the tiles don't generate until you get closer to them.

01:44:54.700 --> 01:44:55.680
That was a little weird.

01:44:55.760 --> 01:44:56.780
I really liked that.

01:44:56.780 --> 01:45:03.500
Yeah, I think – I thought that that was actually like one of the most impressive things about this game because that's your line of sight, right?

01:45:03.980 --> 01:45:08.280
Yeah. You only – the black tiles are just things you can't see.

01:45:08.420 --> 01:45:10.640
So if you're – and it does it pretty accurately.

01:45:10.940 --> 01:45:20.360
If you're in front of something, you know, like a doorway, you'll see like a wedge from the doorway looking out of the doorway but you can't see directly to the sides of like the walls.

01:45:20.820 --> 01:45:25.240
It does it on the overall too where you – it covers things that your characters wouldn't be able to see.

01:45:25.920 --> 01:45:27.120
That's fun, right?

01:45:27.240 --> 01:45:29.940
But it's like – it's weird in 2D.

01:45:30.300 --> 01:45:31.420
Like those aren't my eyeballs.

01:45:32.040 --> 01:45:33.820
I can see that, you know?

01:45:33.960 --> 01:45:37.140
I guess. But it's trying to immerse you in like what this – you're that character.

01:45:37.160 --> 01:45:41.580
So like yeah, you're seeing his perspective but like – you're right.

01:45:41.580 --> 01:45:49.740
It is an element that they should have probably implemented some things, things that are hiding somewhere or stuff that you can't see around a corner.

01:45:49.900 --> 01:45:53.720
But the only time that that would happen happens in like the dungeons which are 3D anyways.

01:45:54.000 --> 01:45:57.160
But I still was very impressed with the fact that they made it work so well.

01:45:57.540 --> 01:46:01.320
Like yeah, it would be nice if there was stuff like hiding in the areas you can't see or something.

01:46:01.580 --> 01:46:05.700
And this is still like a system that is used in like CRPGs today.

01:46:05.700 --> 01:46:13.840
Like the isometrics – like you will have a line of sight that when you move around things will appear to you.

01:46:13.900 --> 01:46:17.960
And like that fog of war needs to be sort of cleared.

01:46:19.260 --> 01:46:26.640
And I think that while it isn't as well implemented as it could have been like you said, Joe, there are still like hidden things around.

01:46:26.640 --> 01:46:29.920
Like there's a casino in a town that's like hidden around a corner.

01:46:30.980 --> 01:46:44.540
Like when you're walking around the castle, there are some places that you sort of have to – you sort of have to explore to find that in any other –

01:46:44.540 --> 01:46:54.000
if it was just like the screen is just the screen and you see past walls and stuff like that could have sort of spoiled your exploration of it.

01:46:55.320 --> 01:47:00.020
Like you just move over a couple pixels and oh, there's that other thing.

01:47:00.540 --> 01:47:07.940
So I think it's not a perfect implementation of it, but I think that it did add to the experience of the game.

01:47:08.680 --> 01:47:10.600
Yeah, that's right. I forgot about stuff like that.

01:47:10.740 --> 01:47:16.320
And I know we're talking about the towns right now, but even on the overworld map, that line of sight thing like mountains block towns.

01:47:16.500 --> 01:47:19.580
You have to go around the mountains to then see like what's over there and stuff.

01:47:19.580 --> 01:47:24.220
Yeah, it did make it so you can't just know exactly where to go just by looking at like the screen.

01:47:24.560 --> 01:47:28.980
You have to actually go where your character would have to go in order to see these things.

01:47:29.180 --> 01:47:30.320
And I think that makes sense.

01:47:30.460 --> 01:47:36.600
Like I do like the line of sight thing and I actually didn't know that that's something that's still implemented in CRPGs.

01:47:38.760 --> 01:47:48.300
It's kind of – I'd like to try it on a new isometric style game because to me it was just disorienting being in –

01:47:48.900 --> 01:47:50.460
Yeah, when it's just these blocks.

01:47:50.480 --> 01:47:51.480
Being like top down.

01:47:51.800 --> 01:47:58.960
Yeah, exactly. Like the fact that it's not – there's not enough graphics to like convey that well and it looks more like a loading error to me.

01:47:59.060 --> 01:48:01.180
I'm glad you guys appreciated it, you know.

01:48:01.320 --> 01:48:13.820
But to me it looked more like, you know, that feature in Super Mario Brothers 3 where like you can see the first – you can see the last line of pixels behind you as well.

01:48:13.820 --> 01:48:16.360
You know, it's like, okay, there has to – they have to do that.

01:48:16.360 --> 01:48:17.580
Oh, it definitely fell into that too.

01:48:18.060 --> 01:48:19.260
Yeah. But yeah.

01:48:19.680 --> 01:48:21.280
Yeah, I thought the same thing when I first saw it.

01:48:21.300 --> 01:48:23.660
My gripe is not with the towns themselves, I want to be clear.

01:48:23.700 --> 01:48:31.700
I actually thought the towns were pretty fun to explore and just like wander around because that was – that was the real world building and storytelling, right?

01:48:31.820 --> 01:48:34.660
Like it wasn't – it wasn't really happening on the overworld.

01:48:34.700 --> 01:48:36.160
It was happening in these towns.

01:48:36.160 --> 01:48:42.500
And like Sean mentioned, that hidden casino and stuff like that, like that builds some character into a game that was needing it.

01:48:43.020 --> 01:48:44.400
So I appreciate all that stuff.

01:48:44.540 --> 01:48:46.420
I just couldn't get over the –

01:48:46.420 --> 01:48:48.040
The presentation of it.

01:48:48.040 --> 01:48:51.420
The disparity of like, yeah, of like, okay, I have eyes.

01:48:51.560 --> 01:48:54.200
They have eyes. Our eyes are not looking at the same thing.

01:48:54.200 --> 01:48:56.040
So why am I – why am I limited?

01:48:58.460 --> 01:49:03.100
I think that the towns themselves had a good amount of character.

01:49:03.100 --> 01:49:11.300
Like there's one that's basically a forest and it doesn't look like the rest of them.

01:49:15.860 --> 01:49:23.640
The individual NPCs definitely do sort of like – there are many copies of them in each town.

01:49:23.880 --> 01:49:30.840
Like I kept coming across this little girl that kept telling her – that kept telling me not to forget about her, which I thought was kind of creepy.

01:49:30.840 --> 01:49:39.100
But other than that, I think this is pretty robust for this age.

01:49:40.120 --> 01:49:48.720
I'll say that I do agree that the towns – like there were a couple of unique ones with like – yeah, there was the forest town.

01:49:48.880 --> 01:50:03.340
That was kind of cool. But as far as like the – I don't know, the functionality of the towns, not all of them, but a lot of them felt not different than any of the other towns.

01:50:03.420 --> 01:50:04.960
You know what I mean? Like they felt like –

01:50:04.960 --> 01:50:07.680
Yeah, visually. It didn't mean too much to get to a new town.

01:50:07.860 --> 01:50:10.000
Yeah. Like no, visually and functionally.

01:50:10.000 --> 01:50:11.960
Like I go into a town and I'd be like, oh, great.

01:50:12.000 --> 01:50:15.880
I'm in a new town. I can buy mostly the same things in most of the towns.

01:50:16.040 --> 01:50:20.340
There are some exceptions. And I can rest up.

01:50:20.640 --> 01:50:23.540
But there was not like – I don't know.

01:50:23.920 --> 01:50:30.080
I like to equate things to Pokemon because it's for like most people – most people that's like a common ground for a lot of people.

01:50:30.300 --> 01:50:35.320
So like in Pokemon, I'll be like, okay, I need to go to the move deleter.

01:50:35.320 --> 01:50:37.280
So like that's Blackthorn City.

01:50:37.520 --> 01:50:39.160
And I know Blackthorn City because it's this.

01:50:39.240 --> 01:50:44.080
But like, okay, now I got to get this item and I got to go to this lavender town, which is like a ghost town.

01:50:44.240 --> 01:50:46.120
There's all these ghost references and all this other stuff.

01:50:46.360 --> 01:50:52.020
Whereas this just felt like, okay, so there's that town to the west and it's got a name and it's a town and it does all the things that the town does.

01:50:52.120 --> 01:50:53.780
And there's a town in the south and it's got a name.

01:50:54.000 --> 01:50:55.500
That's true. And it does all the things that towns do.

01:50:55.660 --> 01:50:57.080
And there were like one or two exceptions.

01:50:57.280 --> 01:51:00.220
There was like Dawn, which you have to use the moon gate to get to it.

01:51:00.300 --> 01:51:01.420
You can get more really powerful weapons.

01:51:01.880 --> 01:51:04.400
And yeah, there was the forest town.

01:51:04.780 --> 01:51:07.620
But for the most part, I was always like, okay, I just need to get to a town.

01:51:07.720 --> 01:51:08.880
I got to rest up. I got to get to a town.

01:51:09.020 --> 01:51:10.700
Like it's really the only thing I ever used towns for.

01:51:10.900 --> 01:51:11.840
Yeah, I agree.

01:51:12.280 --> 01:51:23.340
But I would say that like while they aren't as unique as like a lavender town or like just towns in RPGs that have.

01:51:23.340 --> 01:51:24.360
Yeah, even like Final Fantasy.

01:51:25.880 --> 01:51:28.980
Yeah, like towns that have like unique landmarks.

01:51:28.980 --> 01:51:29.880
Like it does not have that.

01:51:30.000 --> 01:51:34.660
But they do have different configurations of like what is available.

01:51:34.880 --> 01:51:38.620
Like some places don't have a weapon slash armor shop.

01:51:38.740 --> 01:51:40.280
Some places don't have a bar.

01:51:40.480 --> 01:51:44.200
Some places don't have a grocer.

01:51:44.200 --> 01:51:51.500
So like depending on what you need, you do still need to think about like which town is the nearest that can accommodate you.

01:51:53.120 --> 01:51:56.660
Because they're like the nearest one may not have what you need.

01:51:56.820 --> 01:51:57.680
They'll always have an in.

01:51:58.020 --> 01:52:04.560
But other than that, I think that it's sort of a random grab bag of what's available.

01:52:05.080 --> 01:52:08.840
Yeah. In what world does the town not have a grocer?

01:52:09.080 --> 01:52:10.720
I'm not saying that that is realistic.

01:52:11.360 --> 01:52:14.640
I know. I'm just saying like that's another – that's a problem though, right?

01:52:14.800 --> 01:52:21.620
Like I get like, you know, oh, these guys only sell this kind of armor and if you want this armor, you should go to this town.

01:52:21.800 --> 01:52:23.480
Like fine with that.

01:52:23.480 --> 01:52:24.640
That all checks out for me.

01:52:25.360 --> 01:52:30.720
But, you know, this is the kind of game where I was honestly only expecting one town and that's like that's the challenge, right?

01:52:30.820 --> 01:52:33.380
Like you always have to go back to the first town.

01:52:33.540 --> 01:52:35.800
Like you could imagine something like that happening.

01:52:35.920 --> 01:52:37.220
I'm glad they didn't do that.

01:52:37.220 --> 01:52:46.000
But, you know, there is something strange about necessary things to press on and not having those available to you.

01:52:46.600 --> 01:52:58.480
Yeah. And I will say that because of my eventual reliance on a walkthrough that I probably did miss out on whether or not there was a good like – I don't know.

01:52:58.480 --> 01:53:10.940
But you guys tell me was there a good like level of using NPCs to kind of get – gather data and figure out what to do next or – the couple times I would talk to random NPCs, I would get like very little to no information.

01:53:11.840 --> 01:53:13.480
But then I kind of stopped doing that.

01:53:13.760 --> 01:53:30.620
I'd say that if you're using a walkthrough, like a lot of the stuff that comes – that's related to like digging up – like I forget what the thing – the horn or like the sword.

01:53:31.080 --> 01:53:36.480
Like if you were to then talk to a bunch of NPCs, you'll get hints on like how to do that.

01:53:37.980 --> 01:53:45.060
Like a lot of them do give like – compared to other games, relatively valuable hints.

01:53:45.340 --> 01:53:47.980
But if you're using a walkthrough, you're probably not going to run into that.

01:53:48.340 --> 01:54:03.060
Right. Well, I mean I can't even imagine a hint that would come up in one of those however many character text boxes that gives me any information that would help me get like that – the mystic armor, which is on like a random island in a random unmarked spot that you have to know.

01:54:03.060 --> 01:54:04.980
Yeah, I'm not saying that it's very specific.

01:54:08.280 --> 01:54:09.720
It's the mystery of it though.

01:54:09.880 --> 01:54:11.900
It's the – you know, it's some of its flavor text.

01:54:21.700 --> 01:54:41.880
It's the mystery of it.

01:54:41.900 --> 01:54:44.040
Yeah, right, yeah. Where this thing exactly is.

01:54:44.460 --> 01:54:46.060
That's why I feel like there's a happy medium.

01:54:46.060 --> 01:55:01.300
Plus, there's a level of like – I think my expectations also stem a little bit from like more – not even modern games, but like later games than on the NES where it's like, oh, there's like conversations that – there's actually a story being told and I can figure it out based on the story.

01:55:01.300 --> 01:55:06.560
I can figure out where to like guess, where to start guessing, like educated guesses based on the story.

01:55:06.900 --> 01:55:16.100
Rather than when it's here where it's just like a vague hint that like you would take hours and hours of just guesswork to figure out what they're talking about.

01:55:16.280 --> 01:55:17.960
I don't – and again, I don't even know if that's how it was.

01:55:18.100 --> 01:55:22.860
That's just how I was imagining it because most of the people I spoke to were like, welcome to Montour West.

01:55:23.240 --> 01:55:25.340
Or like, don't forget about me.

01:55:25.500 --> 01:55:27.320
Or like, go to Ambrosia.

01:55:27.480 --> 01:55:30.260
And I'm like, what? I didn't even know that Mondain died.

01:55:31.400 --> 01:55:34.720
Did you guys go to the hospitals to give blood to get gold?

01:55:35.740 --> 01:55:42.360
I tried once and party members were too close to death to be any use.

01:55:42.520 --> 01:55:43.680
So I just decided not to.

01:55:44.640 --> 01:55:49.800
Yeah, I think you have to be pretty close to full health if not full health to like really use the system.

01:55:50.280 --> 01:55:53.120
But what was I going to say?

01:55:53.920 --> 01:56:00.020
That's like a good way to get some gold because, you know, your blood.

01:56:00.020 --> 01:56:02.300
Like in real life, stuff's valuable.

01:56:03.600 --> 01:56:05.360
So sell your blood.

01:56:05.580 --> 01:56:08.520
Like this game could just be you living in a town.

01:56:08.880 --> 01:56:14.360
