01:56:24.680 --> 01:56:26.000
I got to go give some blood.

01:56:26.460 --> 01:56:27.300
That's typical fantasy.

01:56:27.300 --> 01:56:32.260
Also, there's pretty advanced doctors for like they're doing blood transfusions or like.

01:56:32.360 --> 01:56:33.420
They just want the blood.

01:56:33.680 --> 01:56:35.700
Yeah, I guess so. Well, maybe.

01:56:35.840 --> 01:56:39.000
Yeah, that's true. Maybe there's some spell that they use it for.

01:56:39.400 --> 01:56:41.600
Yeah, maybe it's like Exodus hates blood.

01:56:41.980 --> 01:56:43.180
You're just trying to get away.

01:56:43.300 --> 01:56:46.720
You know, like they're like, oh, we're going to make circles around the whole town with your blood.

01:56:47.200 --> 01:56:50.820
Exodus, by the way, not the character on the box art.

01:56:50.820 --> 01:56:53.680
Not that devil Satan like character.

01:56:53.900 --> 01:56:55.320
Exodus is a giant.

01:56:57.220 --> 01:57:02.900
Well, it's actually I was going to say machine, but they describe it in the manual as neither human or machine.

01:57:03.620 --> 01:57:05.360
So I thought it was the island.

01:57:05.580 --> 01:57:07.000
I thought the island was Exodus.

01:57:07.500 --> 01:57:10.420
Right. I guess it's just like it's an ominous thing.

01:57:10.540 --> 01:57:14.080
Like it's like you can't really describe it.

01:57:14.160 --> 01:57:16.140
Right. Is it the island or is it like the spirit?

01:57:16.600 --> 01:57:17.560
Within the island.

01:57:17.840 --> 01:57:18.920
The presence. Yeah, exactly.

01:57:19.040 --> 01:57:24.480
I don't know. I guess, you know, I read the I read the manual once and then just play the game.

01:57:24.740 --> 01:57:29.620
So, well, Exodus is the creation of Minax and Mundane.

01:57:29.820 --> 01:57:31.740
I think one and two.

01:57:31.920 --> 01:57:35.220
Yeah. Ultima one and two, which is that's also really cool.

01:57:35.340 --> 01:57:38.640
Like all of a sudden, that's some pretty cool stuff for a game I've been ragging on.

01:57:38.780 --> 01:57:42.220
Like, you know, the idea that it's not a man or a machine.

01:57:42.220 --> 01:57:48.160
It's it's a presence and that it was created by and it was created by the villains of the previous two.

01:57:48.160 --> 01:57:50.240
But again, that's our words.

01:57:50.400 --> 01:57:51.200
That's not the game.

01:57:51.380 --> 01:57:52.400
I don't know if it's a presence.

01:57:53.820 --> 01:57:55.280
Yeah. Is it just like a place?

01:57:56.000 --> 01:58:02.940
I thought it was. I like the idea that like I like the idea that like I'm going to start like dramatizing things that I'm talking about.

01:58:03.040 --> 01:58:04.080
I'm talking about my water bottle.

01:58:04.260 --> 01:58:06.300
I'll tell someone like it's neither human nor machine.

01:58:06.800 --> 01:58:09.480
Like it's just like anything that's not human or machine.

01:58:09.960 --> 01:58:13.520
It's just like the, you know, the grass is not human nor machine.

01:58:13.820 --> 01:58:15.520
That's right. Exodus was a water bottle.

01:58:15.620 --> 01:58:18.760
I forgot about that. Is a water bottle technically a simple machine?

01:58:18.940 --> 01:58:19.880
Like it's a container.

01:58:19.880 --> 01:58:20.760
Nah, it's just a thing.

01:58:20.820 --> 01:58:22.320
I don't think so. Yeah.

01:58:22.700 --> 01:58:24.380
I mean, it's screwed. There's a lid that screws on.

01:58:24.540 --> 01:58:25.660
That's kind of. The bottle itself.

01:58:25.660 --> 01:58:33.940
I don't know who beat the I don't know who beat the game here, but it's important to mention that Exodus does not like challenge you to a fight.

01:58:34.160 --> 01:58:35.240
You to defeat him.

01:58:35.360 --> 01:58:38.860
You have to like solve a bunch of puzzles that he's set up for you.

01:58:40.220 --> 01:58:43.980
I didn't do it, but that sounds pretty fun and stupid.

01:58:44.500 --> 01:58:51.360
Like the end of a game where like the whole thing was you grinding combat and now it's like solve a bunch of puzzles if you want to beat me.

01:58:51.500 --> 01:58:53.180
It's like. It's really not even solve the puzzle.

01:58:53.180 --> 01:58:58.200
It's like just write down what the time Lord said to you and then do that.

01:58:59.140 --> 01:59:05.260
And then you walk out and I think the like the island falls into the sea.

01:59:05.580 --> 01:59:07.140
We're spoiling the game.

01:59:07.960 --> 01:59:09.660
And then it cuts to credits.

01:59:10.920 --> 01:59:14.280
The old Banjo-Kazooie fairy godmother route.

01:59:14.580 --> 01:59:16.680
Got it. No idea what that means.

01:59:16.760 --> 01:59:20.480
Classically. Right before Exodus, you also have to fight the floor.

01:59:20.740 --> 01:59:22.140
The floor? Yeah.

01:59:22.140 --> 01:59:23.800
It's just. The floor is lava?

01:59:25.060 --> 01:59:33.040
I assume that there's actually like characters there that just are the exact same sprite as the repeated tile of the floor.

01:59:33.740 --> 01:59:34.680
Is that what happened?

01:59:34.680 --> 01:59:36.080
Is that what that is? I'm confused.

01:59:36.800 --> 01:59:42.160
Yeah. There's like a battle where it looks like nothing's there, but there's a bunch of enemies you can't see because they are the floor.

01:59:42.240 --> 01:59:43.640
Wow. I did not get to this part.

01:59:44.340 --> 01:59:45.300
I didn't either.

01:59:46.140 --> 01:59:49.360
But I saw that. Now, Joe, I like your explanation, but I don't think it's true.

01:59:49.420 --> 01:59:54.520
I think you are quite literally fighting the floor from what I understand of the Ultima wiki.

01:59:55.460 --> 01:59:59.680
Well, my explanation was more of what I thought was like technically what the game was doing.

01:59:59.960 --> 02:00:01.620
Oh, gotcha. That's probably happening.

02:00:01.620 --> 02:00:04.520
There are enemies that are like just the same tile as the floor.

02:00:05.020 --> 02:00:07.840
Yeah. Because you do have to fight specific spots.

02:00:07.960 --> 02:00:10.720
You can't just like be like, get on your hands and knees and strike this thing.

02:00:10.960 --> 02:00:13.480
Are we sure it's not ghosts? Like maybe it's just invisible things?

02:00:13.820 --> 02:00:14.980
It's called floor.

02:00:15.760 --> 02:00:17.160
The wiki was pretty clear.

02:00:17.340 --> 02:00:21.720
All right, whatever. It's also I watched somebody beat it and I think like the name of the enemy.

02:00:21.820 --> 02:00:22.720
Did the enemies have names?

02:00:22.820 --> 02:00:24.800
I can't remember. But for some reason I knew it was floor also.

02:00:25.060 --> 02:00:37.480
Yeah, they had names. I would like to see like this campaign actually ran as like a D&D module where the DM has to say like how –

02:00:38.440 --> 02:00:42.180
describe how you're attacking the floor and how the floor is attacking you.

02:00:43.120 --> 02:00:44.240
I don't know. Yeah.

02:00:44.240 --> 02:00:50.620
I mean I think it's pretty funny because now you're making me guess like was it the floor or was it invisible enemies?

02:00:50.880 --> 02:00:53.780
Like theoretically like there is no wrong answer, right?

02:00:53.780 --> 02:00:56.440
I love how much we've been stuck on this floor thing.

02:00:57.040 --> 02:01:00.560
Yeah. It kind of sounds like you're like slowly losing your mind as you're –

02:01:00.560 --> 02:01:04.000
Well, it's just like who thinks the floor is a good final boss?

02:01:04.200 --> 02:01:08.860
I know. Well, second, you know, the penultimate boss.

02:01:09.000 --> 02:01:14.120
But like I don't know. I never expect the floor but I guess that's no different than that hand in Legend of Zelda.

02:01:14.240 --> 02:01:15.400
That will grab you.

02:01:17.320 --> 02:01:20.820
If you're handmaster or whatever and they're not looking at you.

02:01:20.940 --> 02:01:23.840
It's bizarre. But it's this giant hand that just comes down from the ceiling.

02:01:23.980 --> 02:01:24.860
It's crazy creepy.

02:01:25.560 --> 02:01:28.040
But, you know, that's also like who thought of that?

02:01:28.280 --> 02:01:29.740
I think hand works better than floor.

02:01:31.060 --> 02:01:32.580
Okay. Yeah. Maybe.

02:01:32.920 --> 02:01:33.940
The floor is Exodus.

02:01:34.880 --> 02:01:35.820
You are the floor.

02:01:36.460 --> 02:01:38.240
You've been the floor the whole time.

02:01:38.700 --> 02:01:45.240
One last thing I want to explain is that we keep referencing this exploit that apparently we all used to make the game a lot easier.

02:01:45.260 --> 02:01:50.640
And I feel like maybe we should just let the listeners know exactly what that was to kind of get a better handle.

02:01:51.440 --> 02:01:52.500
So – No, that's the mystery.

02:01:52.620 --> 02:01:53.620
We're the NPCs in this game.

02:01:53.620 --> 02:01:57.200
Right, right. Well, the NPCs don't talk about the exploit.

02:01:57.500 --> 02:01:59.460
You know, that's – It would be funny if they did though.

02:02:00.520 --> 02:02:04.360
But basically you can't get your pirate ship.

02:02:04.440 --> 02:02:07.680
You can't steal a pirate ship I think until level five.

02:02:07.920 --> 02:02:08.860
Yes. You're level five.

02:02:08.920 --> 02:02:15.600
Correct. But once you get past level two, from that point on every time you go up levels you're going to get harder and harder enemies.

02:02:15.660 --> 02:02:17.720
And that's when the game gets like really, really difficult.

02:02:17.720 --> 02:02:25.500
So what the exploit is and why I had so many party members but also – it wasn't the only reason I had so many party members.

02:02:25.680 --> 02:02:28.780
But you make like a sacrificial party.

02:02:29.600 --> 02:02:34.260
You get enough money and experience to level them up to level five.

02:02:34.760 --> 02:02:36.420
Go get your pirate ship.

02:02:36.740 --> 02:02:39.860
And then as soon as you have the pirate ship, go save.

02:02:40.240 --> 02:02:41.980
Restart the game.

02:02:42.200 --> 02:02:46.300
And I don't know if you have to delete those characters.

02:02:46.300 --> 02:02:48.780
I did but you might not even have to.

02:02:48.920 --> 02:02:52.780
But I delete those characters and get new fresh level one characters.

02:02:53.240 --> 02:02:55.680
All the enemies on the screen go back to being like level one.

02:02:56.000 --> 02:03:01.540
And no enemies will appear in the water which the game intends for you to run the enemies in the water.

02:03:01.720 --> 02:03:05.420
Because by the time you can get the ship enemies, you're at a high enough level where enemies appear in the water.

02:03:05.600 --> 02:03:12.380
So the game stays very easy but you have access to – not very easy but the game stays easy and you have access to everywhere in the game.

02:03:12.380 --> 02:03:18.180
Definitely not the way it was intended but I honestly can't imagine enjoying playing it the way it was intended.

02:03:18.300 --> 02:03:25.200
It also adds a lot more grinding than we ever needed to but that's neither here nor there.

02:03:25.200 --> 02:03:28.920
Well, you mean if we had not done the exploits?

02:03:28.920 --> 02:03:36.840
Well, I think it balances out with like not running into those other creatures and having the rest of the game be easier.

02:03:37.040 --> 02:03:42.140
But it's still like – it's more grinding before you can do your thing.

02:03:42.160 --> 02:03:43.420
You know what I mean? Sure.

02:03:43.480 --> 02:04:04.020
Yeah. But – so for one – I didn't test this to see how true it was but from what I was reading in the guide that gave me the idea for this exploit, it was saying that like trust me, it takes way less time to max out your level when you're at level one and fighting low level enemies than fighting high level enemies that have higher experience rewards but take way longer than like –

02:04:04.020 --> 02:04:05.280
Ah, I see. Than it would take.

02:04:05.580 --> 02:04:13.180
So they were – you know, that and like I think there was one other source that said like it's going to take you way longer to play this game if you do it the right way.

02:04:13.380 --> 02:04:26.680
Yeah, I think all speedruns take advantage of that too and it's just something – it's funny because like you saying that we didn't talk about it, Joe, is just – it's like one of those things where we just assumed.

02:04:26.840 --> 02:04:28.040
Yeah, it's like that's the game.

02:04:28.560 --> 02:04:30.680
The other way is the weird way to play the game.

02:04:30.680 --> 02:04:31.640
Yeah, exactly.

02:04:31.840 --> 02:04:36.060
Like that's the way to play the game but also like do you want people to know the exploit?

02:04:36.340 --> 02:04:37.840
Should they decide that on their own?

02:04:37.980 --> 02:04:53.440
Like there's so many things around this but it's like I can't – I can't think of any other example like this because it's not really – it's not really like a cheat code and it's not really like a mechanic that was intended.

02:04:53.780 --> 02:04:59.020
It's – it's – you know, it's not quite like the warp zone worlds in Super Mario Brothers where you're like, oh, don't tell people about that.

02:04:59.120 --> 02:05:00.360
They have to discover that on their own.

02:05:00.360 --> 02:05:12.220
Like I don't know how to feel about the exploit system other than knowing that like all three of us without talking to each other felt it necessary to use it.

02:05:13.560 --> 02:05:14.420
Right, right.

02:05:14.980 --> 02:05:23.180
You know, I think it's just like one of those things everybody decides at some point while they're playing this game like, you know, maybe I want to do this instead.

02:05:23.460 --> 02:05:25.740
Like maybe I want to find a way to play this game a little bit easier.

02:05:25.740 --> 02:05:29.680
Right. And there are exploits in other games that, you know, that ruin the challenge of the game.

02:05:29.840 --> 02:05:33.760
In this game, I think the exploit – personally, I think the exploit makes it a better game.

02:05:33.760 --> 02:05:46.280
The І

02:06:11.120 --> 02:06:15.680
So, you know, there are nine numbered

02:06:15.680 --> 02:06:16.540
Ultima games.

02:06:16.760 --> 02:06:17.700
We technically played

02:06:17.700 --> 02:06:20.000
the third one, but they struck the three out of it.

02:06:20.720 --> 02:06:21.840
And I say nine

02:06:21.840 --> 02:06:23.720
because seven was split into

02:06:23.720 --> 02:06:25.820
two parts. It was Ultima 7 Part 1

02:06:25.820 --> 02:06:27.460
and Ultima 7 Part 2, so

02:06:27.460 --> 02:06:29.840
that's technically just, like, the same game,

02:06:29.940 --> 02:06:31.320
but we'll just say nine.

02:06:31.640 --> 02:06:33.800
The last of these games was released in

02:06:33.800 --> 02:06:34.600
1999.

02:06:35.320 --> 02:06:36.800
Wow. That's pretty crazy.

02:06:36.800 --> 02:06:37.740
It's been, like, an

02:06:37.740 --> 02:06:39.260
absence of Ultima

02:06:39.260 --> 02:06:41.580
for two decades now.

02:06:41.680 --> 02:06:43.520
Yeah, I mean, I know that, like,

02:06:43.520 --> 02:06:45.800
Ultima is, like, one of those

02:06:46.940 --> 02:06:47.980
founding RPG

02:06:48.640 --> 02:06:49.540
series, like,

02:06:49.620 --> 02:06:51.000
it spawned

02:06:53.280 --> 02:06:55.400
genres. Like, Ultima Underworld

02:06:55.400 --> 02:06:57.820
pretty much created, like, what would

02:06:57.820 --> 02:06:59.660
become, like, the first person RPG

02:06:59.660 --> 02:07:01.240
and, like, the immersive sim.

02:07:02.320 --> 02:07:04.080
And then you got Ultima Online,

02:07:04.460 --> 02:07:06.920
which was... Was it the first MMO?

02:07:07.100 --> 02:07:08.260
I don't quite remember.

02:07:08.740 --> 02:07:09.680
No, I think that...

02:07:09.680 --> 02:07:11.240
Wasn't that EverQuest? Maybe it was EverQuest.

02:07:11.320 --> 02:07:13.560
I'm not sure. But, um...

02:07:13.560 --> 02:07:15.420
It has a legacy, but

02:07:15.420 --> 02:07:16.860
it's crazy that...

02:07:16.860 --> 02:07:19.240
I had no idea that there were no newer

02:07:19.240 --> 02:07:20.920
ones, or at least in this century.

02:07:22.240 --> 02:07:24.080
Well, since you brought up Ultima

02:07:24.080 --> 02:07:26.220
Online, I want to share

02:07:26.220 --> 02:07:28.500
two really funny stories that...

02:07:28.500 --> 02:07:29.340
You know, because it's Ultima.

02:07:29.400 --> 02:07:30.780
It's an Ultima episode. Might as well.

02:07:32.020 --> 02:07:33.980
Online games, MMOs, you know,

02:07:34.060 --> 02:07:34.980
they have a

02:07:36.020 --> 02:07:37.920
fandom behind them, and there's a lot of

02:07:37.920 --> 02:07:40.180
different rules, and Ultima, like, to pride itself

02:07:40.180 --> 02:07:42.280
on the systems it creates

02:07:42.280 --> 02:07:44.060
and just sticking to those systems.

02:07:44.860 --> 02:07:46.280
So, long before they

02:07:46.280 --> 02:07:48.460
invited players into the game,

02:07:48.460 --> 02:07:49.860
they were creating this world

02:07:51.060 --> 02:07:54.140
that, like, had a vegetation system.

02:07:54.260 --> 02:07:55.240
Oh, I know this story.

02:07:55.600 --> 02:07:56.620
And, like, animals. Yeah.

02:07:57.020 --> 02:07:58.040
You know? And

02:07:58.520 --> 02:08:00.300
the creators of the games had no idea

02:08:00.300 --> 02:08:01.720
that the player base would just

02:08:01.720 --> 02:08:03.300
kill everything.

02:08:03.500 --> 02:08:04.520
Destroy the ecosystem.

02:08:04.840 --> 02:08:06.260
You know, whether it was, like...

02:08:06.260 --> 02:08:08.680
Right, exactly. Just, like, I want to kill all the bears

02:08:08.680 --> 02:08:10.060
whether they attack me or not.

02:08:10.220 --> 02:08:12.000
And in doing so,

02:08:12.180 --> 02:08:13.180
by killing, like,

02:08:14.380 --> 02:08:15.500
anything, you know,

02:08:15.620 --> 02:08:16.540
that happened to Rome,

02:08:16.720 --> 02:08:17.600
they destroyed

02:08:17.600 --> 02:08:18.980
the vegetation system

02:08:19.620 --> 02:08:20.680
in the game.

02:08:21.120 --> 02:08:22.320
And therefore,

02:08:22.360 --> 02:08:24.820
it was like, okay, now we actually can't

02:08:24.820 --> 02:08:25.900
have this system

02:08:25.900 --> 02:08:27.540
because these are necessary things

02:08:27.540 --> 02:08:28.380
that need to survive.

02:08:28.620 --> 02:08:29.820
So, after, like,

02:08:30.140 --> 02:08:32.380
trying to, like, combat it by, like,

02:08:33.000 --> 02:08:34.000
fixing spawn points

02:08:34.000 --> 02:08:34.900
and doing stuff like that,

02:08:35.060 --> 02:08:36.100
eventually they just had to

02:08:36.600 --> 02:08:38.320
just scrape the whole system

02:08:38.320 --> 02:08:39.820
and start a new one

02:08:39.820 --> 02:08:42.140
that just was, like, these things will just spawn

02:08:42.940 --> 02:08:44.260
regardless of anything.

02:08:44.500 --> 02:08:46.360
You know? Like, they don't need to reproduce.

02:08:46.360 --> 02:08:47.500
They don't need to have

02:08:47.500 --> 02:08:48.960
these things living around them.

02:08:49.040 --> 02:08:49.860
They'll just happen.

02:08:50.160 --> 02:08:51.500
So, I thought that was pretty funny.

02:08:51.500 --> 02:08:52.480
I love it. Because, like,

02:08:52.560 --> 02:08:54.120
the game never needed that.

02:08:54.260 --> 02:08:55.320
But it was...

02:08:55.320 --> 02:08:57.440
Right. I love when games have these systems

02:08:57.440 --> 02:08:59.480
for very tertiary reasons.

02:08:59.920 --> 02:09:01.620
But I guess that also explains

02:09:01.620 --> 02:09:02.820
why we can't have nice things.

02:09:02.820 --> 02:09:04.760
And it's relevant to Ultima 3.

02:09:05.160 --> 02:09:07.080
You know? It's like, there's so many things

02:09:07.080 --> 02:09:08.220
in this game that's like,

02:09:08.320 --> 02:09:09.720
I'm not a fan of it,

02:09:09.800 --> 02:09:10.760
but, hey, it's there.

02:09:10.760 --> 02:09:12.560
And they chose to include

02:09:12.560 --> 02:09:14.100
those things as, like,

02:09:15.280 --> 02:09:18.200
you know, systems that somebody could use

02:09:18.200 --> 02:09:20.040
to potentially exploit

02:09:20.040 --> 02:09:22.920
or to immerse themselves further.

02:09:23.740 --> 02:09:24.760
There's a lot of, like,

02:09:25.800 --> 02:09:27.000
optionality in playing

02:09:27.000 --> 02:09:29.540
both Ultima 3 and MMOs.

02:09:29.600 --> 02:09:32.320
So, I see the parallel. Now, Lord British,

02:09:32.820 --> 02:09:34.120
okay, who is the creator

02:09:34.120 --> 02:09:35.260
of Ultima's,

02:09:35.320 --> 02:09:37.240
that's his in-game alter ego,

02:09:38.120 --> 02:09:40.640
he appeared in Ultima Online

02:09:40.640 --> 02:09:42.580
and was killed

02:09:42.580 --> 02:09:46.560
during an in-game beta test

02:09:46.560 --> 02:09:48.700
